2. Why is Aggregation called "Weak HAS-A"?

The main reason is independence, not just sharing.

Suppose:

Teacher t =
    new Teacher("Alex");

Now:

Department it =
    new Department("IT", t);

Department cs =
    new Department("CS", t);

Memory:

Alex Teacher Object
        │
        ├── IT Department
        │
        └── CS Department

Same Teacher object is shared.

Now delete IT Department:

it = null;

Question: Does Alex Teacher disappear? -> No.

Question: Does CS Department still use Rahul? -> Yes.

Because Teacher exists independently.

---------------------------------------

Why Weak?

Because Department does NOT own Teacher.
Department only stores: reference.

Teacher teacher;

Teacher was created outside:

Teacher t =
    new Teacher("Alex");

So:

Delete Department ❌
Teacher still exists ✔

This makes the relationship weak.